  "base_commit": "971eaea0615e153f697b86b0c20db35077f1300e",
  "scope": "Cup scene scale, reveal and shuffle-slot names; animation, rendering and input locals; stale comments and formatting.",
  "changes": [
    "Rename mOnes to mCupScale, mFlags to mRevealRequested, mIds to mCupAtSlot and mSwap0/mSwap1 to mSwapSlotA/mSwapSlotB. Preserve all field types, widths and offsets.",
    "Name the cup identity, shuffle-pair selection, random draws, touch coordinates, animation duration and OAM output variables according to their explicit uses.",
    "Remove stale comments claiming raw accesses or casts absent from the baseline. Explain the actual render indexing and preserve the existing control flow and matching constraints."
  ],
  "evidence": {
    "scale": "Each scale initializes to 0x1000 and is adjusted by cup y relative to the shuffle midpoint. Cup_DrawOamList calls func_02053200 before rendering; that helper implements the Fix12 reciprocal through cstd::reciprocal_async and fdiv_result.",
    "reveal": "StateSetup clears the request, StateSelect sets it for the touched cup, StateResult sets it for the remaining cups and InitResources sets all. Cup_UpdateAnim selects animations1/4 when clear and2/5 when set, distinguished further by cup contents. The field names the animation request, not instantaneous openness.",
    "slots": "mCupAtSlot maps resting shuffle positions to cup identities. mSwapSlotA/B select those positions from the existing pair tables. Completing a swap or triggering its fake-out exchanges the mapped identities.",
    "render": "Render sorts cup identities by descending y. Position/content/animation selection use cup identity, while mFrame uses draw-order index. This existing distinction remains exactly as compiled.",
    "ownership": "Queue23 state e405c968eab0f6c2beb845907ca6d2e92c024400 has no active Cup class/file/range conflicts. Production ov006 ranges: text0x020de988..0x020e0638, init0x021303d0..0x021304ac, ctor0x0213358c..0x02133590, bss0x02141870..0x021418b0.",
    "runtime_validation": "No new emulator experiment required: the names follow explicit accesses, arithmetic and helper implementation. These are descriptive reconstructed names, not claims of recovered original spelling.",
    "retained_constraints": [
      "Keep Cup_UpdateAnim split0x5000 bases and per-path reset index assignments, CupFx_Update distinct frame spellings, the byte-pointer sparkle decrement and the full fake-out angle assignment.",
      "Keep separate render x/y address spellings, fixed-point ABI calls, manual factory lifecycle, pragmas, scopes and gotos.",
      "mSparkleShuffles has no setter in this translation unit; no unsupported explanation was added. CupFx_Update subtracts six raw fixed-point units from y, not six pixels."
    ]
  },
